        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">overflow</code> (and longhand variants) set how overflow is handled - such as by overflowing (visible), hiding or clipping to the bounding container, or clipping and adding scrollbars.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Prior to CSS Module 4 this was ignored for replaced elements (such as images) that overflow their container. In CSS Module 4 replaced elements should do as other elements: <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#overflow-control\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#overflow-control</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Support was added for FF148 in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1999100\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1999100</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Support was added for Crhome in 108 - <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5137515594383360\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5137515594383360</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari doesn't support this yet - ran this test code on latest browserstack hosted browser and you can see that the image is clipped to the circle <a href=\"https://codepen.io/therealpaulplay/pen/JoGQogd\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://codepen.io/therealpaulplay/pen/JoGQogd</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a subfeature to <code class=\"notranslate\">overflow</code> and its longhands.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3805373106\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42744\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42744/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42744\">mdn/content#42744</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29002",
            "title": "FF148 CSS overflow respected for replaced elements",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-09T23:42:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-09T04:28:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
