        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Address is the dev-doc-needed requirements of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2012727\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2012727</a> \"action.isEnabled() throws instead of returning the global enabled state\" by, under <code class=\"notranslate\">isEnabled</code>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>adding <code class=\"notranslate\">details</code> and moving the information for <code class=\"notranslate\">windowID</code> under it.</li>\n<li>adding <code class=\"notranslate\">tabID</code> and indicating it's available in Chrome only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related content changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3887257311\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42997\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42997/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42997\">mdn/content#42997</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28964",
            "title": "Bug-2012727 action.isEnabled updated properties info",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T17:38:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-03T17:37:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF148 Supports using Document.execCommand with option \"paste\" in web content in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998195#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998195#c18</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previously this would only work on extensions. The change is a reimplementation of the feature using the Clipboard API, so shares the same behaviour as added in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699897493\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28587\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587\">#28587</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The feature is non-standard but in its \"kind of\" standard, paste is only supported in extensions. So what we're doing is adding non-standard behaviour to some browsers. What I have done is added an entry for paste that matches <code class=\"notranslate\">copy</code> and similar in versions, then added version notes for this additional \"non-standard\" implementation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3805383037\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42747\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42747/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42747\">mdn/content#42747</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28953",
            "title": "FF148 Document.execCommand with paste supported in content",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-09T06:02:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-02T06:05:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update the Firefox statement for <code class=\"notranslate\">NodeIterator.detach()</code>, indicating that this is still supported.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Verified with collector test, see <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/20829#issuecomment-3811033154\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/20829/hovercard\">this comment</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #20829.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1916130689\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/20829\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/20829/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/20829\">#20829</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28935",
